-- title:
--   E₂ (θ j)^{-(p+1)/2} lies in the level-N function field
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime with $p \ge 5$, let $N \ge 1$ be a natural number with $p \nmid N$, and let $K$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$. Write $\tilde P \in K[[q]]$ for the image under $\mathbb{Z} \to K$ of the power series with constant coefficient $1$ and $n$-th coefficient $-24\sum_{d \mid n} d$ for $n \ge 1$ (that is, the reduction of $E_2$), regarded inside the field $K((q))$ of Laurent series via the inclusion of power series. Write $\bar\jmath = q^{-1}\cdot(E_4^3\,\eta^{-24}$-numerator$)$ for `jqModC K`, the Laurent series $\mathrm{single}(-1,1)$ times the reduction mod $p$ of `jNum`, and let $\theta$ be the $K$-linear operator $f \mapsto q\,f'$ on $K((q))$, i.e. multiplication by $\mathrm{single}(1,1)$ after formal differentiation. The assertion is that the Laurent series $\tilde P \cdot (\theta\bar\jmath)^{-(p+1)/2}$, the exponent being the integer $-((p+1)/2)$ and the power taken in the field $K((q))$, belongs to `modularFunctionFieldC K N`, the intermediate field of $K((q))/K$ generated by $\bar\jmath$ together with its image $\bar\jmath_N$ under `qExpand K N`.
--
--   This is the membership clause of Robert's theorem B in its function-field formulation: the weight $p+1$ object $\tilde P\,(\theta\bar\jmath)^{-(p+1)/2}$, built from the reduction of the Eisenstein series $E_2$, is a modular function of level $N$. It feeds [`ModularCurve.exists_coe_eq_qP_mul_thetaL_jqModC_zpow_and_stackOrd_eq_zero`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_coe_eq_qP_mul_thetaL_jqModC_zpow_and_stackOrd_eq_zero), where this element is used together with its divisor information.
